<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Godfrey Binaisa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1920">1920</a>–<a href="/years/2010">2010</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Godfrey Binaisa was a Ugandan lawyer who served as attorney general under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milton-obote">Milton Obote</a> in the 1960s and as president of Uganda from June 1979 to May 1980, after the overthrow of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/idi-amin">Idi Amin</a>. Chosen by the National Consultative Council to replace <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yusuf-lule">Yusuf Lule</a>, he was deposed by the Military Commission led by Paulo Muwanga, which then organised the disputed election of December 1980.</p></div>
